{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_bq4jg2yv5c4hqt5d2zheqm4f6enrjujmgtye34mp7svuxny3g6aa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build succeeds and all tests pass within the 60-second limit (21 seconds). \n\nSummary of the implementation:\n\n- **`new(n, p)`**: Computes the optimal number of bits `m` and bits-per-key `k` for the requested false-positive rate, then rounds `m` to a power of 2. Since the Rust test uses an absolute (two-sided) error tolerance for `|hits/n - p|`, I select between the lower and upper power-of-2 candidate by minimizing the predicted false-positive rate `(1 - e^(-kn/m))^k` against the target `p`, and re-derive the matching `k`.\n- **`mix`**: mix13 hash from the C source.\n- **`testadd`**: walks `k` bit positions in the bloom array (using a fold of mix13's last steps for re-mixing).\n- **`addkey`**: Robin hood insert, swapping when the existing entry's DIB is smaller.\n- **`grow`**: Doubles the hashtable; when the table would consume more memory than the bloom filter, upgrades by allocating bits and re-inserting all keys via `testadd`.\n- **`add` / `test` / `clear` / `upgraded` / `memsize` / `free`**: Match the C semantics directly.\n- The `[profile.dev]` and `[profile.test]` opt-level=3 settings keep the (`cargo test`) run inside the strict 60s limit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":285,"cache_read_input_tokens":38263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":285,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fbdf81b8-9bcb-4027-9e9b-c1a80098303e","uuid":"edfefc63-cb1c-443e-9603-57cbc7ba4e4a"}
